1
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:20,280
欢呼与掌声
CHEERING AND APPLAUSE

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:25,440
大家好，我们回来了！我们回来了，
太感谢大家了。
Hello, we're back! We're back,
thank you so much, everybody.

3
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,240
谢谢！谢谢！
Thank you. Thank you.

4
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:34,960
现在，大家都知道，金融危机
正发生在眼前。
Now, as we know, there's a financial
crisis going on at the moment.

5
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:40,000
但我们决定
不参与其中。
But we've decided
not to take part in it.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,160
现在先来点预热
让你们看看
接下来几周的内容。
So, coming up now is a taster
of what you can expect
over the coming weeks.

7
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:52,200
三、二、一，冲！
Three, two, one. Go!

8
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,120
我们可是聪明人，没错。
We're wise men. We are.

9
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,600
哎呀，那是阿尔巴尼亚的土匪！
Crikey, it's the Albanian rozzers!

10
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:14,080
看他怎么摔倒的！
Look at him tumble!

11
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:18,920
我们可能撞到了
一个澳大利亚人，非常严重。
We may have hit an
Australian quite badly.

12
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,920
我们差点把他抓住！
We nearly had him!

13
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,240
我们是不是可以去
找个个子小点的来干？
Couldn't we have murdered
someone a bit smaller?

14
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,600
最高时速？没人知道！
Top speed? Nobody knows!

15
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,760
车门后视镜掉了！
The door mirror has come off!

16
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,520
我觉得他简直是个超级白痴。
I think he could be a massive idiot.

17
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:44,320
连个球都不带弹。
Not even a dribble.

18
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,440
来吧，罗马的拉力赛来了。
Here we go, Roman rallying.

19
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:51,320
我压根不知道它在哪儿。
I don't know where it is.

20
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,160
那个间隙已经够大了。
That gap is big enough.

21
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,880
还挺不错的。
That was quite good.

22
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,440
这只是个开胃菜。
All that is to come.

23
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:13,520
但现在是这个。
我们必须把注意力放在这里。
But this is now. We must turn
our attention to this.

24
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:16,720
这就是罗马尼亚的特兰斯法加拉山道，
我们说过
This is the Transfagarasan Highway
in Romania, and we said

25
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:21,480
几年前我们就说过
它是全世界最棒的道路。
a couple of years ago that this
is the best road in the world.

26
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:25,520
可是，很多美国人说，
而且他们总是自以为无所不知，
However, many Americans say,
and they do tend to know everything,

27
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:30,320
事实上，世界上最好的道路是
弗吉尼亚的蓝岭公路
（就在弗吉尼亚）。
that in fact, the best road in
the world is the Blue Ridge Parkway
in Virginia.

28
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:35,240
于是我们的制片人对我们说
我们随便挑喜欢的车，
So our producers said to us
we should pick any cars we liked,

29
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:37,600
直接去那里试一试。
get over there and try it out.

30
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:41,200
这条路
我们要开上去的。
This is the road
we'll be driving on.

31
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:44,880
蜿蜒的，500英里长的
沥青丝带，
A snaking, 500 mile ribbon
of asphalt,

32
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:48,560
穿梭在孤寂的松林中
以及高耸的山峰。
scything through the lonesome pines
and the soaring peaks.

33
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:53,400
看起来很棒。那我们现在来认识
我们将要用的车子们。
It looks good. So now let's meet
the cars we'll be using.

34
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:59,400
这就是我带来的车。
法拉利458 Italia。
This is what I've brought.
It's the Ferrari 458 Italia.

35
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:05,280
在我看来，
它是他们目前制造的最佳跑车。
It is, in my view,
the best car they currently make.

36
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:08,560
而且你根本没法反驳
这点，克拉克森，
And you can't actually argue
about this, Clarkson,

37
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:13,640
因为你在电视上说过
它是宏伟的
而且是史上最伟大的之一。
because you said on the television
that it was magnificent
and one of the all-time greats.

38
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:19,960
我可以争辩，而且我会争辩，因为
虽然这车很不错，
I can argue, and I will, because
although this is an excellent car,

39
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:23,880
它并没有那么出色
相比我带来的这辆车，
it's not quite as excellent
as the car I've brought along,

40
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:28,120
这就是，梅赛德斯SLS。
which is this, the Mercedes SLS.

41
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:36,400
他们俩都错了，因为我带来的这车是最好的。
They're both wrong,
because I've brought the best car.

42
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:38,720
我带来的是保时捷 911 GT3RS……
I've brought the Porsche 911 GT3RS...

43
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:44,280
……它是最棒的 911，等于是最棒的车。
..which is the best 911,
and therefore the best car.

44
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:46,760
这下结束了，哈蒙德。什么？
That's an end of it. Hammond. What?

45
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:49,960
你带的这玩意儿，跟在枪战里掏刀一样。
What you've brought, mate,
is a knife to a gunfight.

46
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:54,000
这怎么解释？我给你说说，行吧？英超，英超，
How do you make that out?
Let me explain, OK?
Premiership, Premiership,

47
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,840
约翰斯通油漆杯。多少钱？说清楚。
Johnstone's Paint Trophy.
How much is it? Exactly.

48
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:02,080
想想看，价钱只有另外两台的一半。多少钱？10.4万。
You think about it. It's half
the price of the other two.
How much is it? 104,000.

49
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,920
这根本不是一半。
It's not half the price.

50
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:09,160
好吧，基本差不多。你这台多少钱？16万。对。
Well, pretty much. How much is yours?
160. Well, yeah.

51
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:13,200
17万。再装点配件的话？大概19万。完事儿。
170. And by the time you put
anything on it? Well, 190.
There you go.

52
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,320
这台只要一半价钱，却依旧是最好的。
This is half the price
and still the best.

53
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:19,840
不是吧！我们走着瞧。它还贴了贴纸！保时捷竟然……
It's not! We shall see.
It's got stickers on it!
Porsche have given it

54
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:23,400
给它加了点不常见的花哨装饰，这在保时捷身上挺少见。
an unusual little flamboyant touch,
which is rare for Porsche.

55
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:27,960
灰车配红轮毂还行，但刹车卡钳是黄的，真是丢人。
Red wheels on a grey car,
which isn't bad, but the calliper's
yellow, and that looks stupid.

56
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:34,000
对，这颜色灾难！简直是时尚危机啊！
You're right, it's a colour disaster!
It is. Oh, I've gone off it,
It's a fashion crisis(!)

57
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:40,400
我就想说，能在这儿坐镇老前辈，开这么一台成熟的车，真是不错。
Can I just say how nice it is
to be the elder statesman here
with the grown-up car?

58
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:43,160
那车门？“看看我，我是只雄鹰！”
With those doors?
"Look at me, I'm an eagle!"

59
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:48,040
还能按个键让二氧化碳喷出来，还穿上达斯·维德的装束？
Can you get an extra where you hit
a button and CO2 flows out as you get
out in a Darth Vader costume?

60
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,960
承认一下，这车门确实有点炫耀味。
I admit the doors are
a bit show-offy.

61
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:55,040
但我把它关上时，那叫一个优雅。
But when I close them,
that is pure elegance.

62
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:58,000
不，它就是巨无霸，事实如此。
No, that is gigantic, is what it is.

63
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,120
这玩意儿吸引的好像是五岁小孩。
This appeals to someone who's five.

64
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:04,400
你那台吸引的倒像是五十五岁，觉得一分钟后就不行了。
Yours appeals to someone who's 55
and thinks it won't work
in a minute.

65
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:08,520
这台适合有品位、讲究的人……
This is for somebody
who has taste, refinement...

66
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:12,080
不，抱歉，这显然是更现代的车……
No, sorry, it's obvious that
that is a more modern car...

67
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,000
“我们本可以争论到日落，
'We could have argued until sunset,

68
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:20,720
但最后决定直接去蓝岭公园道上来一场狂飙，看哪辆更牛。”
'but decided instead to see
which was best with a blast
on the Blue Ridge Parkway.'

69
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,200
走起！
Here we go!

70
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:44,240
“然而，一出现问题就……”
'However, immediately,
there was a problem.'

71
00:05:46,910 --> 00:05:52,510
兄弟们？对对，那个路标写的是 35 英里每小时限速？
Guys? Yeah? Did that signpost
say 35 mph speed limit?

72
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:08,150
蓝岭公园道全长 469 英里。
The Blue Ridge Parkway
is 469 miles long.

73
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:12,430
不可能全程都是 35 英里每小时，根本不可能！
It can't all be 35 miles an hour.
Can't be!

74
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:14,950
“我说得对，它根本不是。”
'I was right. It wasn't.'

75
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:19,230
现在这里是 25 英里每小时，伙计们。
It's now 25,
25 miles an hour here, chaps.

76
00:06:19,230 --> 00:06:20,790
什么？！
What?!

77
00:06:24,670 --> 00:06:30,790
我确信我们会拐过去，前面还有个十字路口，直接上吧。
I'm sure we'll get round here
and there will be another side
with a cross, just go for it.

78
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:37,870
“但事实上，这条路能开的最快速度也只有 45 英里每小时。”
'But no. It turned out that
the fastest you can ever drive
on this road is 45.'

79
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:48,910
我准备把车调到舒适模式，反正也只能这么开了。
I'm going to put it in the comfort
setting. May as well, really.

80
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:53,470
“这太无望了。于是我们停下来重新思考。”
'This was hopeless.
So we pulled over for a rethink.'

81
00:06:55,790 --> 00:07:00,910
我们现在的难题是，走不了这段路，因为要跑完100码得花上30年。
The problem we've got is
we can't go on because it'll
take us 30 years to do 100 yards.

82
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:04,710
我们不能往那边走，那是北卡罗来纳的森林。
We can't go that way because those
are the woods of North Carolina.

83
00:07:04,710 --> 00:07:08,270
像猪一样尖叫！我可不想像猪一样尖叫。这里全是胡伦人，
Squeal like a piggy! I don't want
to squeal like a piggy.
It's full of Huron,

84
00:07:08,270 --> 00:07:11,070
他们会砍掉你的脑袋。最后的莫希干人。
who'll cut your head off.
Last of the Mohicans.

85
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:14,630
那边，下面……那边到底是啥？
That way, down there...
What's over there?

86
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:16,230
NASCAR 的天下。
NASCAR country.

87
00:07:16,230 --> 00:07:21,830
是吗？全球90%的NASCAR车队都在那视野里。
Is it? 90% of the world's
NASCAR teams are in that view.

88
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:26,790
班乔斯，胡伦人。老男人们，V8，牛排。没错，V8。
Banjos, Huron. Good ol' boys,
V8s, steaks. Absolutely. V8s.

89
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:32,110
我开V8，你也开V8，你们……古典车更棒。就是更棒。
I'll have a V8 and you'll have a V8
and you... Classics, which is
better. It's just better.

90
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:38,300
从 Stannah 电梯高速公路摆脱出来，连詹姆斯都有点疯狂。
'Freed from the Stannah stairlift
highway, even James went a bit mad.'

91
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,620
是啊！
Yes!

92
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,940
FERRARI ENGINE ACCELERATES——声音相当爽！
FERRARI ENGINE ACCELERATES
That's a pretty good noise.

93
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:58,020
PORSCHE ENGINE REVS——那倒不怎么爽。
PORSCHE ENGINE REVS
That isn't.

94
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:01,780
我带来了最好的车。
I've so brought the best car.

95
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:07,940
那台保时捷根本比不了这台，
That Porsche is no match for this,

96
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:13,460
它拥有全球最强的自然吸气发动机。
the most powerful naturally
aspirated engine in the world.

97
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:20,180
不过 SLS 可不止是野蛮的马力。
But there's more to the SLS
than just brute force.

98
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:22,900
它看起来、听起来——
This may look and sound -

99
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:26,260
咕噜！——像一台愤怒的肌肉车，但底层，
GRRR! - like a muscle car, angry,
but underneath,

100
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:29,100
它非常技术化，极具欧洲范儿。
it's very technical.
It's very European.

101
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:34,300
变速箱放在后面以优化配重，而且采用同款双离合，
The gearbox is at the back
for better weight distribution,
and it's the same double clutch,

102
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:38,140
七速箱，跟法拉利在加州用的一样。
seven-speed box Ferrari use
in the California.

103
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:42,100
传动轴采用碳纤维，仅重四公斤。
The driveshaft is made from
carbon fibre, so it only weighs
four kilograms.

104
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:48,020
车身、底盘以及其它部件全是铝制，这车轻得飞起。
The body, the chassis, everything
else is made from aluminium.
This car is very light.

105
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:55,220
这不是超跑，叫做跑车。
This isn't a supercar.
It's a sports car.

106
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:57,340
它被减重、去掉了多余东西。
It's been lightened, stripped out.

107
00:08:57,340 --> 00:09:02,980
牺牲了后排座位，的确。但它让人感觉活力十足。
It sacrifices rear seats, yes.
But it just feels alive.

108
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,980
纯粹、直接、瞬间。
Pure, direct, immediate.

109
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:10,780
另外两台会收获所有赞叹的目光，没错。
The other two are going to get
all the admiring looks, yes.

110
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:13,220
但这就是我的意思。
But that's my point.

111
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:16,300
我开这车不是为了给别人看。
I'm not driving around in this
for other people's benefit.

112
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:20,420
我开这车是因为我热爱驾驶它。完。
I'm driving around in this
because I love driving it. End.

113
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:27,420
与此同时，在高科技法拉利里，那个1947年的老家伙有点吃力。
'Meanwhile, in the high-tech
Ferrari, the man from 1947
was having a bit of a struggle.'

114
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:29,980
詹姆斯，你的方向盘操作得怎么样？
James, how are you getting on
with the steering wheel?

115
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:36,940
你根本不知道它是怎么回事，对吧？
You've no idea
how it works, have you?

116
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:39,980
我不想显得老土或者像卡在泥里，
Don't want to sound old fashioned
or like a stuck in the mud,

117
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:43,740
但你有两个换挡拨片，还有六个
but you've got the two paddles
to change the gears, there are six

118
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:46,780
小开关和按钮在后面控制音响，
little switches and buttons
behind for the stereo,

119
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:50,060
指示灯，它们是方向盘上的两个按钮，前灯，
the indicators, they're two buttons
on the wheel, the headlamp,

120
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:53,660
远近光灯，就在那里，雨刷也在那边，
high and low beam, that's there
and the wipers are there,

121
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:57,220
舒适悬挂模式，
发动机启动按钮——
the comfort suspension setting,
the engine start button -

122
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,460
全部都装在方向盘上。车子其它部位根本没事。
all on the steering wheel. Nothing
for the rest of the car to do.

123
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:03,580
这招还真挺聪明，这就是现代的玩意儿……
That's all very clever,
that is the modern way...

124
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:08,740
‘随着维克托·梅尔德鲁的唠叨，我们
越开越深入北卡罗来纳。
'As Victor Meldrew droned on, we
plunged deeper into North Carolina.

125
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:16,260
‘这里是全世界观赛人数最多的
那项运动的诞生地，
世界第一观赏运动的发源地。
'The birthplace of what is by far
the world's number one
spectator sport.

126
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:18,100
‘NASCAR。’
'NASCAR.'

127
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:23,940
一直想去NASCAR赛道玩玩。
Always wanted to go
to a NASCAR track.

128
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:27,500
‘于是我们去了。
而且还是个相当特别的赛道。’
'So we did.
And a rather special one.'

129
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:33,580
它可不是那种能坐二十五万人、现代化的巨兽。
It's not a modern 250,000 seater
leviathan.

130
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:38,620
它是威尔克斯堡赛道，
美国第一条椭圆形赛道。
It's Wilkesboro Speedway,
America's first oval track.

131
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:41,060
就是在那里诞生了NASCAR。
This is where NASCAR began.

132
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,620
哇！
Wow!

133
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:50,860
废弃的赛道总有种说不清的
阴森感。
There is something desperately
spooky about a disused racetrack.

134
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:54,100
‘这段历史悠久的柏油路
实在太诱人了，
'The historic tarmac
was very tempting,

135
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:58,500
‘而且幸好市长和负责赛道的女士恰好在场，
于是我们请求能不能
'and luckily, the Mayor and the lady
who runs the track were around,

136
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:01,660
‘来玩一把。’
'so we asked if we could have
a little go.'

137
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,260
只要我们保证不闹事…
If we promise to behave ourselves...

138
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:07,100
只要你答应。为了追溯老时光。
If you promise.
Just for nostalgia's sake.

139
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:10,540
举手，我保证…
我保证…我郑重承诺…
Raise your hand. I promise...
I promise... I solemnly promise...

140
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:13,140
我郑重承诺…
I solemnly promise...

141
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,420
要是我撞车，撞到就是撞车…
要是我撞车，撞到就是撞车…
If I wreck, I wreck...
If I wreck, I wreck...

142
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:19,020
要是我挂了，就挂了…要是我挂了，就挂了。
干得好，来个击掌！
If I die, I die... If I die, I die.
You're good. High-five!

143
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:22,700
从没跟市长击过掌啊。
好嘞，伙计们！
Never high-fived a mayor before.
Right, chaps!

144
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:29,020
小小一段路程。
我郑重承诺，举着手说我们
不会开快。
Little drive.
I solemnly promised, with my hand in
the air, that we'd wouldn't go fast.

145
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:32,140
‘可悲的是，我们忘了。’
'Sadly, though, we forgot.'

146
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:35,340
切成sport plus。现在上路！
Put it in sport plus. Now let's go!

147
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,900
LED灯，换挡，没错。
LEDs, change gear, yes.

148
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,020
哦不，我们现在真的在赛车了。
Oh, no, we're now actually racing.

149
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,420
我们是上帝造的最蠢的男人
在这世界上！
We're the thickest men
on God's earth!

150
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:58,580
‘其实我没蠢。
'I wasn't being thick, actually.

151
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:01,340
‘我只是想把詹姆斯
拽进麻烦里。’
'I was trying to coax James
into a problem.'

152
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:04,340
哈蒙德，究竟会发生什么
Hammond, what is it that happens

153
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:09,820
当你在炎热的天气里高速驾驶
法拉利458时？
when you drive a Ferrari 458
very fast on a hot day?

154
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,860
我猜会起火。
I believe it catches fire.

155
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:16,380
是啊是啊，真的只有少数会起火。
Yeah, yeah, only a few
have caught fire.

156
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,860
到目前为止——它才上市几个月——
So far - it's only been
on sale a few months -

157
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:26,100
已有五辆法拉利458
被烧成灰烬
five Ferrari 458s
have burnt to a crisp

158
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:31,220
因为后轮拱的胶水受热过度，
直接把车烧掉。
because the glue in
the rear wheel arches gets too hot
and burns the car out.

159
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:33,500
真想象不到詹姆斯在里面还能放松。
Can't imagine James is relaxing
in there.

160
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,700
谢了啊！（！）
Thanks for that(!)

161
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:41,740
‘因为我的车没起火，杰里米闷得无聊，成了个流氓。’
'Because my car didn't
catch fire, Jeremy got bored
and became a yobbo.'

162
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:44,620
这玩意儿怎么让屁股踢开？
How do you get the arse to kick out
on this thing?

163
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,460
要的！哈哈！
Yes! Ha-ha!

164
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:58,220
这玩意儿只能闹得很糟。
This can only end badly.

165
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:00,940
‘带着必然的结局，它真的就这么了。’
'And with a certain inevitability,
it did.'

166
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,420
天呐！
Christ!

167
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:09,540
干得好，干得好。我看我们已经不需要再开车了。
Well done. Well done. I think that we
don't need to do any more driving.

168
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:15,740
不过，实际上路还长，这意味着我要换掉那条破轮胎。
However, there was in fact a long
way to go, which meant I needed
to replace the ruined tyre.

169
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,780
这辆SLS根本没有备胎。
The SLS doesn't have a spare.

170
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,740
但这时，霍格大佬出面了。
But then, Boss Hogg stepped in.

171
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:24,860
这是罗伯特·约翰逊，北威尔克斯堡的市长。
This is Robert Johnson,
the Mayor of North Wilkesboro.

172
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:26,860
霍华德·迈尔斯，我需要你的帮忙。
Howard Myers, I need your help.

173
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:31,020
你得让汤姆·麦克尼尔回去把轮胎给我们装上
You need to get Tom McNeal
back down to his tyre shop for us

174
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:36,620
给这辆奔驰装个胎。赶紧让他给我打电话，快点。
to get a tyre put on this Mercedes.
Have him call me, chop-chop.

175
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:39,700
我可不指望鲍里斯·约翰逊会帮我们！
I don't think Boris Johnson
would do this for us!

176
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:43,140
我正想说，市长的来电真是让人吃惊！
I was just thinking, that was quite
a surprise call from the Mayor!

177
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:48,260
‘在轮胎店里，装胎的只会说乡巴佬口音。’
'Down at the tyre shop,
the fitter only spoke hillbilly.'

178
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:51,620
我拿到04040，要换它们得用坡道灯才能搞定。
I got 04040, it takes
a ramp lamp to change them.

179
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:55,060
瓦斯尼姆，过去在主街上……
Wassname, used to be on
Main Street...

180
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:58,060
他含糊不清地哼哼唧唧
HE MUMBLES UNINTELLIGIBLY

181
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:02,740
‘大概翻译就是，他手里没有合适的轮胎。’
'Roughly translated,
he didn't have the right tyre.

182
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:06,660
‘于是霍格大佬又打回电话，找到另一个觉得
'So Boss Hogg got back on the phone
and found another man who thought

183
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:08,900
‘他库存里可能有合适的东西。’
'he might have something suitable
in stock.'

184
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:14,260
这些轮子还能装上吗？可以。走吧。路上只有一英里。他还有这些轮胎？
Will they go on those wheels? Yes.
Let's go. It's only a mile down
the road. And he's got these tyres?

185
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:17,620
走吧。怎么的，我们一起走？
Let's go. What, so, like, us go?

186
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:22,140
你就这么把我撂在这？其实我还以为会这么做。
Are you going to just leave me?
I thought I would, actually.

187
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:25,220
是啊，是啊，是啊。像你那样。
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Like you do.

188
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:28,940
我不闹事。你喜欢猎獾诱饵吗？
I don't make a fuss.
Do you like badger bait?

189
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:36,100
没有大猩猩可不一样啊？说真的，这垃圾盖真是……
Not going to be the same
without the big ape, is it?
What a bin lid, honestly!

190
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:37,860
不过他真是个流氓，是吧？
He is a yobbo, though, isn't he?

191
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:41,300
跑四圈就把它玩得乱七八糟。
Four laps and he'd trashed it
just by messing about.

192
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:43,180
他根本不考虑后果。
He doesn't think ahead.

193
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:45,380
我还能听见你，矮子！
I can still hear you, you shortarse!

194
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:53,020
‘当侏儒和书呆子开车前往那晚的旅馆时，’
'While the midget and the pedant
drove on to that night's hotel,

195
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:55,220
‘我把车拐进了第二家轮胎店，’
'I pulled in
at tyre shop number two,

196
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:58,500
‘希望店主说的话容易听懂。’
'where I hoped the owner would be
easier to understand.'

197
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,380
你觉得这办法能行吗？
Do you think this will work?

198
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:05,780
哦，是啊。能行？我这里有个作弊坦克，全部装了线。一次能发射八枚。
Oh, yeah. It will? I got a cheating
tank back here, all wired in.
It'll shoot out eight at one time.

199
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:13,740
‘不过在后面，我碰到一个会说一点英语的男人。’
'However, in the back, I met a man
who did speak a bit of English.

200
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:18,420
‘他解释说，1940年代，最早的NASCAR车手…’
'He explained how, in the 1940s,
the original NASCAR drivers

201
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:22,380
‘一开始是酿私酒的走私者。’
'had started out as bootleggers
running moonshine.'

202
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:26,100
所以说法子就是，装上大马力发动机去甩掉警察？
So the idea was, you put the big
engines to outrun the police?

203
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:28,820
没错，就是这个思路。
Exactly. That was the idea.

204
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:32,980
于是 NASCAR 就这么诞生了，大家开始用他们为…而造的车来比赛。
And then that's how NASCAR was born,
people racing the cars
they'd built for...

205
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:37,220
他们在1947年把那条小土场赛道给整出来。
They built the little dirt track
down there in 1947.

206
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:41,260
这不就是走私们比谁车最快的玩意儿？
And this was for bootleggers to
just see who had the fastest car?

207
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:46,260
看看谁车子最快。他们就是为了甩掉警察才造车的？对，这就是一切的开头？
See who had the fastest car. That
they'd build to outrun the police?
Yeah. That's how it all began?

208
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:48,580
于是他们就开始互相抢车速。
Then they all started racing
each other.

209
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:53,660
‘我正沉浸在当地历史里时，詹姆斯和理查德已经抵达了过夜点。’
'While I was soaking up the local
history, James and Richard had
arrived at the overnight halt.'

210
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:56,380
这可不是汽车旅馆，稍微高大上一点。
It's not a motel.
It's a bit posher than that.

211
00:15:56,380 --> 00:16:01,100
这些别墅居然自带车库，挺不错的。
The villas have actually got
garages on them. That's quite good.

212
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:05,460
Brookside，对吧？我们要进肥皂剧了。赞！
Brookside, isn't it? We're going
to be in a soap opera. Ace!

213
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,940
（收音机里播放音乐）
MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO

214
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:10,860
你们听过这首歌吗？Steve Earle 的《Copperhead Road》。
Do you know this song?
Steve Earle. Copperhead Road.

215
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:14,500
全是讲改装车去运私酒的事儿。
It's all about doing up cars
to run moonshine.

216
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,020
# Copperhead road! #
# Copperhead road! #

217
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,900
# 听见妈妈在哭，我知道不对劲 #
# Heard mama cryin',
knew something wasn't right

218
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:25,100
# 他正带着每周的货物驶向诺克斯维尔 #
# He was headed down
to Knoxville with the weekly load

219
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:28,900
# 你能闻到威士忌在 Copperhead Road 上燃烧的味道…… #
# You could smell the whiskey
burnin' down Copperhead Road... #

220
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:44,180
‘这家轮胎行是我去过最印象深刻的。’
'This was the most memorable
tyre shop I'd ever been to.

221
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:49,340
‘可是他们货架上的任何东西根本装不下梅赛德斯那巨大的轮毂。’
'However, nothing they had
on the shelves would fit
the Merc's massive rims.'

222
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,260
不。 不行。
No. No.

223
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:55,780
这让我只剩下一个选项。
'Which left me
with just one option.'

224
00:16:55,780 --> 00:17:00,820
所以，我现在只能开着一条破轮胎
So, I'm now driving on a ruined tyre

225
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:06,500
115英里外的酒店，那里是制作组给我们预订的，
115 miles to the hotel where we've
been booked into by the producers,

226
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,260
在弗吉尼亚州。
which is in Virginia.

227
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:10,140
可是这在另一州。
Which is in another state.

228
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:20,060
运气好的话，我会在轮胎爆胎时在方向盘上睡着。
With a bit of luck, I'll have
fallen asleep at the wheel
when the tyre bursts.

229
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:25,580
（欢呼掌声）
CHEERING AND APPLAUSE

230
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:29,140
我们稍后再说。
We'll pick that up later on.

231
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:31,900
不过现在，来点新闻时间吧。
But now, it's time to do the news.

232
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:34,780
重磅新闻是——
And the big news is,

233
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:41,180
詹姆斯和理查德都因一台割草机出了大事故。
James and Richard have both had
a horrible accident with a Flymo.

234
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:47,500
不，听着！你们肯定注意到了，我的中年危机已经结束，掉了头发。完蛋了。
No, listen! You must have noticed.
It was the end of my mid-life crisis,
so I lost the hair. I'm done.

235
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,940
你居然觉得这事已经完事儿了，还装成《Adam and the Ants》那套？
And you actually think it's ended,
dressed as Adam and the Ants?

236
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:56,060
他是《Sergeant Pepper》。我已经翻篇。哈蒙德，要是我跑调唱歌，你怎么办？
He's Sergeant Pepper. I've moved on.
What would you do if I sang
out of tune, Hammond?

237
00:17:56,060 --> 00:18:01,220
闭嘴吧，因为那部电影里你像 Ted Nugent，现在倒像 Kojak。
You can shut up, because in that
film, you looked like Ted Nugent
and now you look like Kojak.

238
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,140
它去哪儿了？
Where's it gone?

239
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:10,500
这可是显而易见，先生们，那个据说一直秃到青春期的男人。
It is noticeable, mate. That from
a man, ladies and gentlemen, who
presumably was bald until puberty.

240
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:13,300
谢谢。这在这个季节是传统。
Thank you. It is traditional
at this time of year

241
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:17,140
我们来看看市面上那些优秀的礼品吧
that we take a look at some of
the excellent gift items available

242
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:20,180
这个圣诞，给你身边的车友们一点惊喜。
this Christmas for
the motorist in your life.

243
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:22,740
你在读目录吗？听起来像是啊！
Are you reading from a catalogue?
It sounds that way!

244
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:26,860
正如我们已经说过的，在那部影片里，你是保时捷铁杆粉丝。没错，我是。
As we've established, in that film,
you are a Porsche enthusiast.
Yes, I am.

245
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:32,460
所以我给你准备的，是款保时捷设计的训练鞋。哎呀！
So what I've got for you here is
a Porsche-designed training shoe.
Oh-ho!

246
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:37,980
310英镑。哇！要是保时捷的，系带要加价吧？
£310. Ooh! Presumably, if it is
a Porsche, the laces are extra?

247
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:43,420
哦，对，还有鞋底什么的。‘先生要两只鞋？’
Oh, yes. And the soles and this bit.
"Sir wants TWO shoes?"

248
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:46,420
两只？那要1900块……
Two shoes? That's 1,900...

249
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:50,660
我真的是保时捷粉。你是奔驰粉，对吧？没错，我是。
I am indeed a Porsche fan. You are
a Mercedes fan, are you you not?
Yes, I am.

250
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:54,900
那你会对奔驰让客户去买的那件衬衫感兴趣吧。
You'd be interested in the shirt
Mercedes are encouraging
their customers to buy.

251
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,500
我这儿给你准备了一件。就是这件奔驰衬衫。
I've got one for you here.
Here is the Mercedes shirt.

252
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:01,140
这是一件背心，上面写着‘TRUCKER’。
It's a vest a with "TRUCKER"
written on it.

253
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:07,460
这背心写着‘TRUCKER’。这不是奔驰的。是的，上面写着奔驰。
It's a vest with "TRUCKER" on it.
It's not a Mercedes.
It is, it says Mercedes on it.

254
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:11,420
这就是布鲁斯·威利斯的风格。耶——，卡车妈咪！
It's the Bruce Willis look.
Yippie-kay-ay, mother trucker!

255
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:16,140
或者说是Rab C Nesbitt。啤酒和蛋黄渍要另加价！
Or Rab C Nesbitt.
Beer and egg yolk stains are extra!

256
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:19,500
我宁愿要这个也不想要保时捷车。真的？我也是。
I would rather have that than
a Porsche car. Really? I would.

257
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:22,940
现在，你们都知道车用空气清新剂，
Now, you know those air-fresheners
you can get for cars,

258
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:26,580
总是标榜山露、春风？阿尔卑斯小溪……
and they're always mountain dew and
spring breeze? Alpine stream...

259
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:30,780
其实就是略带香味的，装着‘病’的瓶子。
All they are really is just
mildly scented bottles of sick.

260
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:36,100
要是空气清新剂闻起来像培根，那该多香啊？
Now, how much better would it be if
your air-freshener smelt of bacon?

261
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,700
大家都喜欢……嗯，犹太人、穆斯林以及猪除外。
Everybody likes...
Well, not Jews and Muslims. Or pigs.

